{"parentUuid":"842cd336-d0c3-4225-a41f-c36b88ed2148","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"03fc8cae-52e9-4a93-8f2d-779cfe10641b","agentId":"a5329aa8252bef056","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012pFSrXqZQrPhCmc7BJDMqc","type":"tool_result","content":"{% extends \"base.html\" %}\n{% block title %}Modules — CUORE{% endblock %}\n{% block content %}\n\n<h1>Module registry</h1>\n{% if view == \"live\" %}\n<p class=\"lede\">The 25 of these 126 codes the live link has any Giorgio bus\ndata for at all — bus, target address if known, and how sure that address\nactually is until this car's own VIN confirms it. Only 5 have a confirmed\ntarget today; the rest are known to exist but not yet addressed, or\naddressed on evidence the doc marks unverified. Everything else about each\none still comes from the reference registry beside it.</p>\n{% else %}\n<p class=\"lede\">Every ECU MES can name, with the aliases it prints for each —\nalias sets, Italian node names, and the CTM collision resolved. This is what\nmakes a scan's module list readable rather than a wall of abbreviations.</p>\n{% endif %}\n\n<div class=\"panel\" style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:end;flex-wrap:wrap\">\n  <div class=\"vtabs\" style=\"margin:0\">\n    <a href=\"/modules\" {% if view != \"live\" %}class=\"on\"{% endif %}>Reference &middot; 126</a>\n    <a href=\"/modules?view=live\" {% if view == \"live\" %}class=\"on\"{% endif %}>Live &middot; 5 addressed</a>\n  </div>\n  {% if view != \"live\" %}\n    <div style=\"flex:1;min-width:220px\">\n      <label for=\"filter\">Filter</label>\n      <input id=\"filter\" type=\"search\" data-search data-filter-target=\"#modtable\"\n             placeholder=\"name, abbreviation, bus…\" autocomplete=\"off\">\n    </div>\n    {% if domain %}<a class=\"btn\" href=\"/modules\">All domains</a>{% endif %}\n  {% endif %}\n</div>\n\n{% if view == \"live\" %}\n\n<div class=\"panel tight\">\n  <div class=\"tw\">\n  <table id=\"modtable\">\n 