{"parentUuid":"3fe79bb9-a208-4366-8194-7b1e8d7f4541","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5329aa8252bef056","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cfp3Vd7hxNeucAbemn478","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GgJho6CXCv3Qj2fNFGcSJK","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\modules_bridge.py","offset":1,"limit":50},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1009,"cache_read_input_tokens":187834,"output_tokens":171,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1009},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":171,"cache_read_input_tokens":187834,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1009,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1009,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01GgJho6CXCv3Qj2fNFGcSJK":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\modules_bridge.py","offset":1,"limit":50}},"serverClassifierRequest":"46cae44f-9be9-4882-8f2e-0be650580baf","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfp3VcVzdjru4azVZXTvg","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a1f5e3b0-4375-46c8-8740-97c06225dd59","timestamp":"2026-10-08T03:16:05.722Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"a1f5e3b0-4375-46c8-8740-97c06225dd59","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"761907a8-f494-4249-a04f-9a0889ef0638","agentId":"a5329aa8252bef056","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GgJho6CXCv3Qj2fNFGcSJK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"The module-tree view: MultiEcuScan's Info/Errors/Parameters/Actuators/\n2\tAdjustments breakdown, per module, for one vehicle.\n3\t\n4\tMultiEcuScan shows a car as a tree of modules, each with its own identity,\n5\terrors, live parameters, actuator tests and adjustment history. CUORE's\n6\tlogs and live tooling already know all of this -- it has just never been\n7\tassembled per-module in one place. Nothing here invents data; every field\n8\ttraces to an existing bridge or library:\n9\t\n10\t* **identity** (hardware/software numbers, ISO code, VIN match) -- the\n11\t  latest all-systems SCAN log, via ``mes_bridge.analyze_scan``. A car with\n12\t  no SCAN log in the corpus gets no identity fields, not guessed ones.\n13\t* **errors** -- the corpus-wide classified DTC list from\n14\t  ``mes_bridge.extract_dtcs``, cross-referenced against the dossier's\n15\t  *current* findings (``mes_bridge.workup``'s ``current_picture``) so a\n16\t  code reads as active / cleared-but-unverified / stale rather than just\n17\t  \"seen at some point\".\n18\t* **parameters** -- the public UDS DID catalog\n19\t  (``cuore.live.did_catalog.all_dids``), each with a known-good band from\n20\t  ``known_good_bridge`` where one exists and the last value this car was\n21\t  actually observed to report, from ``cuore.live.store``.\n22\t* **actuators** -- what has been *learned* from a real dealer-tool capture\n23\t  for this VIN (``cuore.live.actuate.list_actuators``), which modules a\n24\t  replay refuses outright (``cuore.live.safety.ACTUATION_BLOCKED_MODULES``,\n25\t  plus anything on CAN-CH), and the exact consent phrase a run would\n26\t  require. Nothing here runs one -- there is no HTTP route for that, by\n27\t  design; ``run_actuator`` exists only as an MCP tool on the ``obd2``\n28\t  server.\n29\t* **adjustments already done** -- the dossier's ``already_attempted`` list.\n30\t\"\"\"\n31\t\n32\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n33\t\n34\tfrom typing import Any\n35\t\n36\tfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\n37\tfrom . import known_good_bridge, mes_bridge\n38\tfrom .errors import NotFound\n39\t\n40\tfrom mes import modules as modules_mod  # noqa: E402\n41\t\n42\tfrom ..live import actuate, did_catalog, safety, store  # noqa: E402\n43\tfrom ..live.addressing import by_code as _addr_by_code  # noqa: E402\n44\t\n45\t#: Statuses in the order a module list should read: worst first.\n46\t_STATUS_RANK = {\"active\": 0, \"cleared_unverified\": 1, \"stale\": 2, \"clean\": 3, \"unknown\": 4}\n47\t\n48\t\n49\tdef _bus_of(abbrev: str) -> str:\n50\t    addr = _addr_by_code(abbrev)"}]},"uuid":"43353706-bcdb-4a1f-8769-a05c042b3b76","timestamp":"2026-10-08T03:16:05.749Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\modules_bridge.py","content":"\"\"\"The module-tree view: MultiEcuScan's Info/Errors/Parameters/Actuators/\nAdjustments breakdown, per module, for one vehicle.\n\nMultiEcuScan shows a car as a tree of modules, each with its own identity,\nerrors, live parameters, actuator tests and adjustment history. CUORE's\nlogs and live tooling already know all of this -- it has just never been\nassembled per-module in one place. Nothing here invents data; every field\ntraces to an existing bridge or library:\n\n* **identity** (hardware/software numbers, ISO code, VIN match) -- the\n  latest all-systems SCAN log, via ``mes_bridge.analyze_scan``. A car with\n  no SCAN log in the corpus gets no identity fields, not guessed ones.\n* **errors** -- the corpus-wide classified DTC list from\n  ``mes_bridge.extract_dtcs``, cross-referenced against the dossier's\n  *current* findings (``mes_bridge.workup``'s ``current_picture``) so a\n  code reads as active / cleared-but-unverified / stale rather than just\n  \"seen at some point\".\n* **parameters** -- the public UDS DID catalog\n  (``cuore.live.did_catalog.all_dids``), each with a known-good band from\n  ``known_good_bridge`` where one exists and the last value this car was\n  actually observed to report, from ``cuore.live.store``.\n* **actuators** -- what has been *learned* from a real dealer-tool capture\n  for this VIN (``cuore.live.actuate.list_actuators``), which modules a\n  replay refuses outright (``cuore.live.safety.ACTUATION_BLOCKED_MODULES``,\n  plus anything on CAN-CH), and the exact consent phrase a run would\n  require. Nothing here runs one -- there is no HTTP route for that, by\n  design; ``run_actuator`` exists only as an MCP tool on the ``obd2``\n  server.\n* **adjustments already done** -- the dossier's ``already_attempted`` list.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\nfrom . import known_good_bridge, mes_bridge\nfrom .errors import NotFound\n\nfrom mes import modules as modules_mod  # noqa: E402\n\nfrom ..live import actuate, did_catalog, safety, store  # noqa: E402\nfrom ..live.addressing import by_code as _addr_by_code  # noqa: E402\n\n#: Statuses in the order a module list should read: worst first.\n_STATUS_RANK = {\"active\": 0, \"cleared_unverified\": 1, \"stale\": 2, \"clean\": 3, \"unknown\": 4}\n\n\ndef _bus_of(abbrev: str) -> str:\n    addr = _addr_by_code(abbrev)","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":276}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a1f5e3b0-4375-46c8-8740-97c06225dd59","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"43353706-bcdb-4a1f-8769-a05c042b3b76","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5329aa8252bef056","attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14810984 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d1b98347-0a56-40e1-b3d9-1661be97e997","timestamp":"2026-10-08T03:16:05.775Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14810984 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"d1b98347-0a56-40e1-b3d9-1661be97e997","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5329aa8252bef056","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cfp3VvbgWSWvEMxL18Bob","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y8EJJAwokQoh7DFgUUdYPf","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\modules_bridge.py","old_string":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\nfrom . import known_good_bridge, mes_bridge\nfrom .errors import NotFound\n\nfrom mes import modules as modules_mod  # noqa: E402\n\nfrom ..live import actuate, did_catalog, safety, store  # noqa: E402\nfrom ..live.addressing import by_code as _addr_by_code  # noqa: E402\n\n#: Statuses in the order a module list should read: worst first.\n_STATUS_RANK = {\"active\": 0, \"cleared_unverified\": 1, \"stale\": 2, \"clean\": 3, \"unknown\": 4}","new_string":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\nfrom . import known_good_bridge, mes_bridge\nfrom .errors import NotFound\n\nfrom mes import modules as modules_mod  # noqa: E402\n\nfrom ..live import actuate, did_catalog, safety, store  # noqa: E402\nfrom ..live.addressing import MODULES as _ADDR_MODULES, by_code as _addr_by_code  # noqa: E402\n\n#: Statuses in the order a module list should read: worst first.\n_STATUS_RANK = {\"active\": 0, \"cleared_unverified\": 1, \"stale\": 2, \"clean\": 3, \"unknown\": 4}\n\n#: ``Dtc.module`` and the dossier's ``ecu_seen`` are MES's own printed strings,\n#: not abbreviations -- \"Engine / ECM\", \"Continental ABS MK C1\", \"Magneti\n#: Marelli IAW 10JA CF6/EOBD Injection (2.0)\". ``modules.normalize_abbrev``\n#: only resolves the first form. This maps the manufacturer/ECU-description\n#: form too, from the one place that already carries both: the live link's\n#: own address table (``cuore.live.addressing``), whose ``name`` is exactly\n#: MES's printed ECU description for each module it addresses.\n_DESC_TO_ABBREV = {addr.name.upper(): addr.code for addr in _ADDR_MODULES}\n\n_WORD_RE = re.compile(r\"[A-Z0-9/]+\")\n\n\ndef _resolve_module(raw: str) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Best-effort: a free-text module string from the log corpus -> abbrev.\n\n    Tries, in order: direct abbrev normalisation (\"Engine / ECM\" style),\n    an exact match against the live link's known ECU-description strings,\n    then a scan for any registered abbreviation appearing as a whole token\n    inside the string (catches MES's own \"Radio frequency hub (RFHUB)\n    Continental\" form). Returns ``None`` -- never a guess -- when nothing\n    matches.\n    \"\"\"\n    name = (raw or \"\").strip()\n    if not name:\n        return None\n    direct = modules_mod.normalize_abbrev(name)\n    if direct:\n        return direct\n    exact = _DESC_TO_ABBREV.get(name.upper())\n    if exact:\n        return exact\n    for token in _WORD_RE.findall(name.upper()):\n        resolved = modules_mod.normalize_abbrev(token)\n        if resolved:\n            return resolved\n    return None"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1278,"cache_read_input_tokens":188843,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1278,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Y8EJJAwokQoh7DFgUUdYPf":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\modules_bridge.py","old_string":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\nfrom . import known_good_bridge, mes_bridge\nfrom .errors import NotFound\n\nfrom mes import modules as modules_mod  # noqa: E402\n\nfrom ..live import actuate, did_catalog, safety, store  # noqa: E402\nfrom ..live.addressing import by_code as _addr_by_code  # noqa: E402\n\n#: Statuses in the order a module list should read: worst first.\n_STATUS_RANK = {\"active\": 0, \"cleared_unverified\": 1, \"stale\": 2, \"clean\": 3, \"unknown\": 4}","new_string":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\nfrom . import known_good_bridge, mes_bridge\nfrom .errors import NotFound\n\nfrom mes import modules as modules_mod  # noqa: E402\n\nfrom ..live import actuate, did_catalog, safety, store  # noqa: E402\nfrom ..live.addressing import MODULES as _ADDR_MODULES, by_code as _addr_by_code  # noqa: E402\n\n#: Statuses in the order a module list should read: worst first.\n_STATUS_RANK = {\"active\": 0, \"cleared_unverified\": 1, \"stale\": 2, \"clean\": 3, \"unknown\": 4}\n\n#: ``Dtc.module`` and the dossier's ``ecu_seen`` are MES's own printed strings,\n#: not abbreviations -- \"Engine / ECM\", \"Continental ABS MK C1\", \"Magneti\n#: Marelli IAW 10JA CF6/EOBD Injection (2.0)\". ``modules.normalize_abbrev``\n#: only resolves the first form. This maps the manufacturer/ECU-description\n#: form too, from the one place that already carries both: the live link's\n#: own address table (``cuore.live.addressing``), whose ``name`` is exactly\n#: MES's printed ECU description for each module it addresses.\n_DESC_TO_ABBREV = {addr.name.upper(): addr.code for addr in _ADDR_MODULES}\n\n_WORD_RE = re.compile(r\"[A-Z0-9/]+\")\n\n\ndef _resolve_module(raw: str) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Best-effort: a free-text module string from the log corpus -> abbrev.\n\n    Tries, in order: direct abbrev normalisation (\"Engine / ECM\" style),\n    an exact match against the live link's known ECU-description strings,\n    then a scan for any registered abbreviation appearing as a whole token\n    inside the string (catches MES's own \"Radio frequency hub (RFHUB)\n    Continental\" form). Returns ``None`` -- never a guess -- when nothing\n    matches.\n    \"\"\"\n    name = (raw or \"\").strip()\n    if not name:\n        return None\n    direct = modules_mod.normalize_abbrev(name)\n    if direct:\n        return direct\n    exact = _DESC_TO_ABBREV.get(name.upper())\n    if exact:\n        return exact\n    for token in _WORD_RE.findall(name.upper()):\n        resolved = modules_mod.normalize_abbrev(token)\n        if resolved:\n            return resolved\n    return None"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"4b5d06fc-c63f-4e49-9ad6-eb8e59a2f62f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfp3VvM3eE5xqF8ZokGna","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"5ee7a713-54b6-46f6-ac35-4d27fecc3cac","timestamp":"2026-10-08T03:16:19.754Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
